  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-31 by an independent auditor who authored none of the change. RFC text (rfc7911): \"A BGP speaker that re-advertises a route MUST generate its own Path Identifier to be associated with the re-advertised route.\" Producers moved in a0589dd1d1, ff2aac12b0 and 30ff1fce91 (RFC 8212 import invalidation). Re-read each: bindSourcePath, recordSection (takeReleased), clearRoutes, recordDeletion, allow, release, retireWrite and writeUpdateBody now carry released-receipt slot retention, policy-epoch fencing and an export-final refusal; a restored or re-announced path keeps the identifier the speaker generated for it (the reservation passes with the released receipt), and none passes the received identifier through or mints one outside forward_path_id.go. forward_path_id.go, forward_body.go, forward_provenance.go and all 19 tagged units are byte-identical, so the positives still require a re-advertised identifier generated per destination and the negatives still fail on a received-id passthrough. Verdict unchanged: enforced. Earlier judgements are in this file's git history.",
